{# The sharing image, as a page for `bin/render-sharing-image` to photograph
   at 1200 × 630. The cover card is the real partial, so name, job title and
   claim cannot drift from the site; only its grid is laid out anew here—the
   portrait at full card height on the left, the domain at the foot of the
   text column. No logo, and nothing that expires.

   The stage is zoomed by 1.6 rather than the type set larger: a chat card
   shows the image about 320 pixels wide, and zooming keeps every measure
   the site's own. The window stays 1200 wide, so the desktop tokens apply.
   The rules below are this page's alone; the stylesheet does not scan this
   file, so a utility written here would not exist. The stage, 750 × 393.75
   at zoom 1.6, is the window size in the script. #}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="de">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <title>Sharing image · Marcel Kraus</title>
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex,nofollow">
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/css/output.css">
    <style>
        html, body { margin: 0; }
        .sharing { position: relative; width: 750px; height: 393.75px; overflow: hidden; zoom: 1.6; }
        .sharing.facade { display: block; min-height: 0; }
        .sharing .cover { position: absolute; inset: 24px 36px; padding: 0; gap: 0; grid-template-columns: 36% 1fr; }
        .sharing .cover-face { width: auto; height: 100%; aspect-ratio: auto; border: 0; border-right: 1px solid var(--color-hair); }
        .sharing .cover-who { padding: 24px 28px 0; align-self: start; }
        .sharing .cover-claim { padding: 0 28px; }
        .sharing .cover-more { padding: 0 28px 24px; align-self: end; }
        .sharing-domain { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.4; color: var(--color-muted); }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="facade sharing" style="--head: 0px;">
        {% embed 'partials/_cover_card.html.twig' %}
            {% block more %}<p class="sharing-domain">www.marcelkraus.de</p>{% endblock %}
        {% endembed %}
    </div>
</body>
</html>
